      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An efficient copper-catalyzed carbenoid insertion reaction of α-diazo carbonyl compounds into Si-H and S-H bonds was developed. A wide range of α-silylesters and α-thioesters was obtained in high yields (up to 98%) from α-diazoesters using 5 mol% of a simple copper(I) salt as catalyst. Using 0.05 mol% of the same catalyst, α-diazoketones led to α-silylketones in low to good yields (up to 70%)."},
